        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="CeNj4uSWV4GNdDWi5vfT-17" value="&lt;br&gt;Each Docx file is picked, and the content of the file is sent to &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;AI &lt;/span&gt;to generate a head-note and extract structured information from the PDF. &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;A.I&lt;/span&gt;. also provides the boundary information where the header section ends.&lt;div&gt;+&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;OUR CUSTOM CODE&lt;/span&gt; will use the information received by &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;A.I.&lt;/span&gt; and process it to attach &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;NEW HEADER SYNTAX&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);&quot;&gt;HEAD NOTE&lt;/span&gt; in the docx file.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="CeNj4uSWV4GNdDWi5vfT-28">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="70" width="480" height="120" as="geometry" />
